---
import AppCTA from '../components/AppCTA.astro';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { vocab, units } from '../lib/learn';

const title = 'How Bol Marathi Teaches: Method & Learning Loop';
const description = 'The Bol Marathi method: themed vocabulary, examples, Hindi bridges, listening, speaking, sentence building and spaced repetition — and what the website vs the app each do.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
	<div class="prose">
		<p class="kicker">Methodology</p>
		<h1>How Bol Marathi teaches</h1>
		<p class="lede">
			One source of truth, two products. The website never invents words —
			everything teachable here comes from the app's curriculum.
		</p>

		<h2>The learning loop</h2>
		<ol class="loop">
			<li><strong>Vocabulary</strong> — words grouped into themes (food, family, travel), because themes are easier to remember than alphabets.</li>
			<li><strong>Context</strong> — every word sits inside its category and lesson, not alone on a list.</li>
			<li><strong>Examples</strong> — each word carries a real Marathi sentence with Hindi and English meanings.</li>
			<li><strong>Listening</strong> — hear the word and pick it out; pronunciation you can't hear, you can't reproduce.</li>
			<li><strong>Speaking</strong> — say real sentences with microphone checks and Marathi voice setup.</li>
			<li><strong>Sentence construction</strong> — arrange words into Marathi's subject–object–verb order until it feels natural.</li>
			<li><strong>Spaced repetition</strong> — reviews arrive before you forget, weakest words first.</li>
			<li><strong>Long-term retention</strong> — streaks, XP, levels and reminders keep the loop turning.</li>
		</ol>

		<h2>Why Hindi → Marathi comparisons</h2>
		<p>
			Hindi speakers already know Marathi's sentence shape and hundreds of
			shared words. Bridge lessons map each Hindi pattern onto Marathi word
			by word, so prior knowledge transfers instead of starting from zero.
			English meanings ride along for everyone else.
		</p>

		<h2>How the curriculum progresses</h2>
		<p>
			{units.length} units × 6 lessons ({units.length * 6} lessons): greetings
			and alphabet first, then survival phrases, everyday vocabulary, sentence
			patterns, pronunciation, questions, postpositions — up through advanced
			grammar, literature, business Marathi and a final assessment. Each unit
			adds vocabulary, speaking, listening, bridges, sentence building,
			grammar and culture.
		</p>

		<h2>What the website provides</h2>
		<p>Discover, understand, read, search, explore: {vocab.length} words, phrases, grammar and all {units.length} units as free study pages. No signup.</p>

		<h2>What the app adds</h2>
		<p>Practice, listen, speak, build, review, remember, track: the interactive loop plus streaks, weakest-word recommendations and reminders. Static pages never pretend to be interactive lessons.</p>

		<p><em>Curated by Bol Marathi. Linguistic review status is tracked openly; uncertain constructions are flagged, not faked.</em></p>
		<AppCTA variant="general" context="method" />
	</div>
</Base>

<style>
	.loop { padding-left: 1.3em; }
	.loop li { margin-bottom: 0.6em; }
</style>
